# ── What never needs to reach a deployment ───────────────────────
#
# The repository carries ~143 MB of source CSVs that the RUNTIME never opens.
# They are inputs to offline builders in `scripts/` — the population build, the
# baseline processors, the awards import — which run on a developer's machine
# and commit small derived JSON into `app/data/`. Shipping the raw inputs to
# Vercel uploaded 143 MB on every deploy to sit unread on the disk.
#
# The rule this encodes is the one the Gravity v4 spec already states: the
# application consumes exported artefacts only, and never reads a source dataset
# during a request. Anything the app genuinely needs lives under `app/data/` and
# is imported, so it is covered by the build and not by this file.
#
# Verified before adding: no file under `app/` references `OtherData`. Every
# reference is in `scripts/`.

# Generated whole-repo dumps for feeding to an LLM. 69 MB, regenerable, and
# stale the moment anything is committed. Also untracked from git in the same
# commit that added this line — they were being versioned.
repomix-output.*

# Brand kits, audit archives and specs. 32 MB, all reference material. The
# brand assets the app actually serves live in `public/brand/`; the reference to
# `docs/cap-and-crease-brand-kitV3` in app/layout.tsx is a comment naming where
# a snippet came from, not a read.
docs/

# Source datasets — offline builder inputs only.
# HistoricalData alone is 133 MB (2008-2024 skaters, lines, teams, goalies).
OtherData/

# Calibration outputs and raw-response caches. The population and stint payloads
# are already gitignored; these entries cover a working tree that has them.
data/gravity-calibration/*/population.json
data/gravity-calibration/*/source-crosswalk.json
data/gravity-v4/
.gravity-calibration-cache/
.gravity-v4-cache/

# Tests and their fixtures never execute in a deployment.
__tests__/
